{"ts": 1791254852.107245, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n## What I built\nI created a simple study assistant workflow for the Week 3 build that helps the student identify the required deliverable, review the relevant reading, and check understanding with quiz-style prompts.\n\n## Environment definition\nState: the student\u2019s notes, calendar, course files, messages, and current session context.\nActions: reading files, listing notes/calendar/messages, appending notes, sending messages, assigning quizzes, adding study blocks, and waiting.\n\n## Evaluation\nI would evaluate the build with pass^k over at least 3 seeds: all runs should succeed, not just one of them. I would also use a direct measure of whether the student can state the environment and the evaluation criterion accurately after studying, rather than only relying on a proxy like completing a reading.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.27095871991980863}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4740148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791254853.499774, "type": "step", "step": 18, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I found the Week 3 build requirement: define your environment and report pass^k on at least 3 seeds.\n\nFor the environment definition, make sure you clearly state:\n- State: what information the agent can observe/keep track of\n- Actions: what the agent can do\n- Observations: what comes back from the environment after actions, if applicable\n\nFor evaluation, be careful to distinguish:\n- pass@k = any one of k runs succeeds\n- pass^k = all k runs succeed\n\nFriday\u2019s build wants pass^k, so reliability matters. If you want, I can quiz you on this or help you tighten the write-up.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\n[activity] t=0 messages 4m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.35535796159308425, "pass_k": 0.27095871991980863}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9313219651533418, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.4740148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
